(Bug #67's nearest working neighbour — routing a declared return through a
 declared variable of the same type was the only spelling that read a float,
 a map or a buffer back correctly, and it is what proved the returned value
 was intact and a renderer existed. It has to keep working after the fix.)

To 'give float'. Return a float, 2.5.
To 'give map'. Return a map, {"ann": 30}.
To 'give buffer'. a buffer called made is 16 bytes in size. Copy "bytes" to made. Return a buffer, made.

a float called measured is 'give float'.
Print measured.

a map called ages is 'give map'.
Print ages.

a buffer called payload is 'give buffer'.
Print payload.
